---
import:
  - undying-tide-base
  - undying-tide-presentation
  - undying-tide-creatures
requires:
  - regeneration
  - upgrade-visuals
description: Scenery - the seabed, background and small fish of each level, and the currents of the waves; the top module, holding the whole game.
---

***definitions***

- :Scenery: is the landscape drawn in a :Level: - its seabed, its background and the small fish swimming in it - seen but never touched.

***implementation reqs***

- :Implementation: builds the 3D :Scenery: of a :Level: in `src/game/render/scenery.ts` and mounts and updates it in `src/game/render/scene.ts` in the 3D coordinate system (`scene.x = x` across `0..1280`, `scene.z = y` across `0..720`, and vertical height `scene.y` from `0` at the seabed floor to `260` at the water ceiling), with no wall meshes around the :Level: (no `cavern-wall`, no `water` backdrop plane mesh `userData.kind = "water"`, and no `darknessShell` cylinder wall mesh `userData.kind = "darknessShell"`), and with a circular, indefinitely spanning seabed floor mesh (`THREE.BufferGeometry` built as a polar disc centred at `(640, 360)` with radius `SEABED_RADIUS = 50000` px so the circular ocean floor spans indefinitely to the camera's far clip and fades smoothly into the underwater fog in every direction), using `src/game/render/glb-loader.ts` to load `public/models/coral-a.glb` and `public/models/coral-b.glb` for corals, `public/models/kelp.glb` for kelp stalks, `public/models/rocks.glb` and `public/models/rock-large.glb` for rocks and rock arches, `public/models/anemone.glb`, `public/models/starfish.glb` and `public/models/clam.glb` for seabed props, `public/models/anchovy.glb` (`Armature|Swim`) for sunlit and twilight background fish schools, `public/models/anglerfish.glb` (`Fish_Armature|Swimming_Normal`) for the lone midnight background fish, and lit 3D meshes (`THREE.MeshStandardMaterial`) for the circular 3D seabed terrain floor (`scene.y` in `0..20`), hydrothermal vents, rising bubbles and :Wave: current streaks, laid out by a hash of the :RunSeed: and the :Depth:, never by the :RunSeed: generator; the :Scenery: is not part of the simulation state or :StateSnapshot:.
  - Every colour of the :Scenery: comes from the palette's `scenery` section, transcribed into `src/game/palette.ts` with the rest of the palette, at the opacities the palette notes.
  - In `src/game/render/scene.ts` and `src/game/render/wave-figures.ts`, the wave current figure (`group.position` at `toScene(wave.x, wave.y)` on the horizontal `XZ` plane), Wide sting ring and Fragment magnet motes all use the 3D coordinate system `toScene(x, y, z)`.
  - :UnitTests: of `src/game/render/scenery.ts` and `src/game/render/scene.ts` assert that neither `buildScenery` nor `buildLevelScene` creates any `cavern-wall`, `water`, `darkness` or `darknessShell` meshes, that `buildScenery` builds the circular `seabed` disc mesh with `THREE.MeshStandardMaterial` centred at `(640, 360)` with radius `50000` (`boundingBox.min.x <= -49000`, `boundingBox.max.x >= 49000`, `boundingBox.min.z <= -49000`, `boundingBox.max.z >= 49000`, and `scene.y` in `0..20`, with every boundary vertex lying on the circle of radius `50000` around `(640, 360)`), places corals, kelp, rocks, vents, seabed props and rock arches on the seabed floor with `position.z` in `40..680` and `position.y >= 0`, rises bubbles vertically in `position.y` (`0..260`) with `position.z` in `40..680`, swims background fish across `position.x` with `position.y` in `60..220` and `position.z` in `60..660` (calling `updateGlbAnimation` on each fish member in `update(seconds)`), and attaches `.glb` models via `src/game/render/glb-loader.ts` (`userData.glbModel`).

- :Implementation: renders the 3D :Scenery: backdrop of :TitleScreen: and the scoreboard page on the Three.js backdrop canvas in the same layer as the drifting motes, beneath all page content: the canvas has a negative `z-index`, or the content is positioned with a `z-index` above it.

***functional specs***

# level-scenery
Each :Level: is drawn in `src/game/render/scene.ts` with its 3D :Scenery: (`buildScenery` mounted in the scene and updated on every frame), with no wall meshes in or around the :Level: (no `cavern-wall`, no vertical `water` plane at `z = -320`, and no `darknessShell` cylinder wall), and like the rest of the :Level: fading into the underwater fog towards the edge of the :Glow:.
- No part of the :Scenery:, the vent halos included, shows beyond the :Glow:.
- The :Scenery: is only drawn: nothing collides with it, and it changes no position, timing, placement or score.
- No part of the :Scenery: props is drawn inside the rectangle from `(0, 0)` to `(300, 290)` that :Hud: covers, or inside the control legend's rectangle from `(0, 580)` to `(260, 720)`.
- The same :RunSeed: and :Depth: always draw the same :Scenery:, and while `tick` stands still the :Scenery: stands still.
- While a :Level: is dived into, its :Scenery: is shifted with it; :RegenerationScreen: shows the :Scenery: of the :Level: as it stood at the :RunEnd:.

# seabed
The :Scenery: has a circular 3D seabed terrain floor (`THREE.MeshStandardMaterial`) across the bottom of the 3D ocean, built as a circular polar disc centred at `(640, 360)` with radius `50000` px so the circular land spans indefinitely into the horizon in all directions (with 3D elevation contours between `scene.y = 0` and `scene.y = 20` derived from `720 - seabedAt(x, ridge)` over `260..1280` and undulating gently across the circular floor, so the player never sees a square corner or an edge of the land anywhere); what grows and rests on it sits on the seabed surface (`position.y` at the seabed height) spread across the floor with `position.x` in `260..1280` and `position.z` between `40` and `680`, attaches its `.glb` 3D model via `attachGlbModel` in `src/game/render/glb-loader.ts` (recording `userData.glbModel`), and follows the palette's water band of the :Depth:.
- Sunlit: sand in the palette's sand colour, 3 to 4 coral heads (`public/models/coral-a.glb`) in its coral colour, 5 to 7 kelp stalks (`public/models/kelp.glb`) in its kelp colour, 120 to 220 px tall, and 2 to 3 seabed props (`public/models/starfish.glb`, `public/models/clam.glb` and `public/models/anemone.glb`) in the coral colour.
- Twilight: sand giving way to 3D rocks (`public/models/rocks.glb`) in the rock colour from left to right, 3 to 4 kelp stalks (`public/models/kelp.glb`) in the kelp-dark colour, 80 to 140 px tall, 2 to 3 soft corals (`public/models/coral-b.glb`) in the coral-soft colour, and 1 to 2 seabed props (`public/models/starfish.glb` and `public/models/clam.glb`) in the coral-soft colour.
- Midnight: sand-deep ground with ridges of 3D rocks (`public/models/rocks.glb` and `public/models/rock-large.glb`) in the rock-dark colour, 1 to 2 soft corals (`public/models/coral-b.glb`), no kelp.
- Abyss: sand-deep ground with rock-dark 3D rocks (`public/models/rocks.glb` and `public/models/rock-large.glb`) and 2 to 3 3D hydrothermal vents in the vent colour, each a chimney 40 to 70 px tall with a 3D halo sphere of radius 30 in the vent-glow colour whose opacity rises from 20% to 40% and back once every 3 s.
- Each kelp stalk sways in 3D: a wave running from its foot to its tip, 0 px across at the foot and 12 px at the tip, once every 4 to 6 s, each stalk at its own point of the cycle.
- Coral, rocks, starfish, clams and seabed anemones stand still.

# scenery-background
Across the 3D cavern, the :Scenery: has 3D rock arches (`public/models/rock-large.glb` via `attachGlbModel`) standing on the seabed with `position.z` in `40..680`, rising 3D bubbles with `position.y` rising from `0` to `260` and `position.z` in `40..680`, and background fish (`public/models/anchovy.glb` and `public/models/anglerfish.glb` via `attachGlbModel`, animated with `updateGlbAnimation`) swimming across `position.x` at vertical height `position.y` in `60..220` and cavern depth `position.z` in `60..660`, as many as the palette's water band of the :Depth: gives.
- Sunlit and twilight have 1 to 2 3D rock arches (`public/models/rock-large.glb`) in the rock-far colour, opaque, 120 to 200 px tall, standing on the seabed between `scene.x = 320` and `1240`; midnight and abyss have none.
- 3D bubble spheres of radius 1.5 to 4 px in the bubble colour at 30% opacity rise from the seabed (`scene.y = 0`) to the top of the cavern (`scene.y = 260`), swaying up to 3 px to either side, and come back in at the seabed after leaving at the top: 10 at sunlit, 8 at twilight and 5 at midnight, rising at 20 to 40 px/s, 10 to 20 px/s at midnight; at abyss each vent gives off a plume of 6, rising at 25 to 45 px/s from its top.
- Every bubble rises at a `scene.x` between 310 and 1270, so none crosses the rectangle :Hud: covers.
- Background fish in the fish colour swim straight across the cavern at 30 to 50 px/s, at vertical height `scene.y` between 60 and 220 and cavern depth `scene.z` between 60 and 660, facing the way they swim, each coming back in at the side it left from after 4 to 8 s: 2 schools of 5 anchovies (`public/models/anchovy.glb`, 10 px long) at sunlit, 1 school of 3 anchovies (`public/models/anchovy.glb`, 10 px long) at twilight, 1 lone anglerfish (`public/models/anglerfish.glb`, 18 px long) at midnight, none at abyss.

# page-scenery-backdrop
:TitleScreen: and the scoreboard page at `/scoreboard` show the 3D :Scenery: of :Depth: 1 behind their content, over the sunlit water gradient, with no darkness and no figure of the :Level:.
- The 1280×720 :Level: is scaled to the window's width, its bottom edge on the window's bottom edge; the sunlit water continues above it to the top of the window, and a window wider than 16:9 shows the :Level: cut off at the top.
- It is laid out as for a :RunSeed: of 1, so both pages show the same :Scenery: every time they open.
- Its kelp sways, its bubbles rise and its fish swim as in a :Level:, timed apart from any :Run:.
- On :TitleScreen: the drifting motes are drawn over it; the scoreboard page gets no motes.
- The page content stays above it, and both pages still fit in the window without scrolling.

# wave-currents
Each :Wave: is drawn on the horizontal `XZ` cavern plane (`group.position` at `toScene(wave.x, wave.y)`) as streaks of current flowing through its circle in its direction, above the seabed and beneath every figure, and like the rest of the :Level: faded by the fog outside the :Glow:.
- 14 streaks, each a rounded line 30 to 60 px long and 2 px wide in the palette's bubble colour, run along its direction at its strength, clipped to its circle, each coming back in at the far side after leaving.
- While it warns the streaks fade in from clear to 20% opacity over the 1 s; while it pushes they are at 50% opacity times its push over its strength, rising and falling with the push.
- Its edge is a soft ring 3 px wide in the bubble colour, fading in to 30% opacity over the warning and out over the last 0.5 s of the push.
- The streaks' lengths and starting places come from a hash of the streak's index alone, never from the :RunSeed: generator, so every :Wave: of a :Level: draws the same streaks.
- A :Wave: is only drawn: its figure touches nothing, and while `tick` stands still it stands still.
